  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-encrypted-blind",
    "description": "OpenID4VCI completion (live) for an issuer response encrypted to a client-held key: credential_response_encrypted true, no credential values, no credential_metadata.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc"
            }
          ],
          "credential_response_encrypted": true,
          "refresh_token": "rt-test-value",
          "dpop_jwk": "{\"kty\":\"EC\",\"crv\":\"P-256\",\"x\":\"test\",\"y\":\"test\",\"d\":\"test\"}",
          "dpop_key_id": "dpop-key-1"
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "notes": "The server relayed the issuer's JWE unread, so credentials[] entries carry no credential value and the completion carries no credential_metadata (a seed, if any, reached the client inside the JWE it decrypted itself). The client pairs credentials[0] with the first credential it decrypted; a count mismatch is an error. refresh_token, dpop_jwk and dpop_key_id are secrets: none is retained in any replay buffer. Values are test values."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-credential-metadata-deferred-display",
    "description": "OpenID4VCI deferred completion: plain issuer response, display-only credential_metadata, no credential_response_encrypted.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc",
              "credential": "o2d2ZXJzaW9uYzEuMA"
            }
          ],
          "credential_metadata": {
            "display": [
              {
                "name": "Employee Card",
                "locale": "en"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "notes": "Plain (unencrypted) response: credential_metadata carries only the display-only members (display, claims). credential_response_encrypted is absent, so credentials[] carry their values."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-replayed-redacted",
    "description": "Replayed OpenID4VCI completion: refresh_token, dpop_jwk and dpop_key_id withheld, listed in redacted_members.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc"
            }
          ],
          "credential_response_encrypted": true,
          "redacted_members": [
            "dpop_jwk",
            "dpop_key_id",
            "refresh_token"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "notes": "Sent only from a replay buffer (Last-Event-ID or resume). The client must treat every listed member as not recoverable: no inferring that the issuer sent none, no inventing a refresh token or DPoP key; an issuance that required one is re-issued, and the credential cannot be renewed without re-issuance."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-plain-seed-refused",
    "description": "Negative: org.siros.secret_seed in the credential_metadata of a plain (unencrypted) completion.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc",
              "credential": "o2d2ZXJzaW9uYzEuMA"
            }
          ],
          "credential_metadata": {
            "org.siros.secret_seed": {
              "nym": "00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "must_refuse": true,
    "notes": "A seed is never relayed in a completion. A server fails the issuance when a plain issuer response carries one and never emits this shape; a client that receives it MUST refuse the issuance and store nothing from it."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-encrypted-seed-leaked-refused",
    "description": "Negative: an encrypted-response completion that relays org.siros.secret_seed in credential_metadata.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc"
            }
          ],
          "credential_response_encrypted": true,
          "credential_metadata": {
            "org.siros.secret_seed": {
              "nym": "00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "must_refuse": true,
    "notes": "With credential_response_encrypted true the server never relays credential_metadata, least of all a seed: the seed stays inside the JWE the client decrypts. A client MUST refuse this completion and store nothing from it."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-encrypted-metadata-leaked-refused",
    "description": "Negative: an encrypted-response completion that carries credential_metadata at all (display-only).",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc"
            }
          ],
          "credential_response_encrypted": true,
          "credential_metadata": {
            "display": [
              {
                "name": "Employee Card",
                "locale": "en"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "must_refuse": true,
    "notes": "credential_metadata is never present when credential_response_encrypted is true; the client uses the response-level credential_metadata it decrypted."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-encrypted-credential-value-refused",
    "description": "Negative: an encrypted-response completion that carries a credential value.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
          "session_id": "ses-a1b2c3d4"
        },
        "flow_id": "flow-vci-001",
        "result": {
          "credentials": [
            {
              "format": "mso_mdoc",
              "credential": "o2d2ZXJzaW9uYzEuMA"
            }
          ],
          "credential_response_encrypted": true
        }
      }
    },
    "expected_response": null,
    "must_refuse": true,
    "notes": "The server cannot read an encrypted response, so a credential value in this completion cannot come from the issuer; the client MUST refuse it."
  },
  {
    "id": "flow-vci-complete-replayed-refresh-token-only",
    "description": "Replayed completion where only refresh_token and dpop_key_id were present on the live one and are withheld.",
    "conformance_level": "flows",
    "input": {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "wmp.flow.complete",
      "params": {
        "wmp": {
          "version": "0.1",
